        },
        {
          "text": "and Jacob the father of Joseph, the husband of Mary, and Mary was the mother of Jesus who is called the Messiah.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MAT.1.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MAT.1.16"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "b"
      },
      "items": []
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "lf"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "17",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "MAT 1:17"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "17",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Thus there were fourteen generations in all from Abraham to David, fourteen from David to the exile to Babylon, and fourteen from the exile to the Messiah.",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "s1"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "text": "Joseph Accepts Jesus as His Son",
          "type": "text"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "18",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "MAT 1:18"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "18",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "This is how the birth of Jesus the Messiah came about",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MAT.1.18",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MAT.1.18"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ": His mother Mary was pledged to be married to Joseph, but before they came together, she was found to be pregnant through the Holy Spirit.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MAT.1.18",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MAT.1.18"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "19",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "MAT 1:19"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "19",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Because Joseph her husband was faithful to the law, and yet",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MAT.1.19",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MAT.1.19"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "did not want to expose her to public disgrace, he had in mind to divorce her quietly.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MAT.1.19",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MAT.1.19"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "20",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "MAT 1:20"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "20",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But after he had considered this, an angel of the Lord appeared to him in a dream and said, \"Joseph son of David, do not be afraid to take Mary home as your wife, because what is conceived in her is from the Holy Spirit.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MAT.1.20",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MAT.1.20"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "21",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "MAT 1:21"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "21",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "She will give birth to a son, and you are to give him the name Jesus,",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MAT.1.21",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MAT.1.21"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "because he will save his people from their sins.\"",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MAT.1.21",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MAT.1.21"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "22",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "MAT 1:22"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "22",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "All this took place to fulfill what the Lord had said through the prophet:",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MAT.1.22",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MAT.1.22"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "23",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "MAT 1:23"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "23",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "\"The virgin will conceive and give birth to a son, and they will call him Immanuel\"",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MAT.1.23",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MAT.1.23"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": "(which means \"God with us\").",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MAT.1.23",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MAT.1.23"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "24",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "MAT 1:24"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "24",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "When Joseph woke up, he did what the angel of the Lord had commanded him and took Mary home as his wife.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MAT.1.24",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MAT.1.24"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "25",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "MAT 1:25"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "25",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But he did not consummate their marriage until she gave birth to a son. And he gave him the name Jesus.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "MAT.1.25",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "MAT.1.25"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
